; Ironhand, for bout(1).  An opponent is a file; this is the whole of
; one.  Adding another means writing another file and nothing else -
; the game reads /lib/bouts and fights whatever it finds.
;
; The header is KEY VALUE lines; after the % come states.  A state is
;
;	state NAME
;		INSTRUCTION
;		...
;
; and the instructions are
;
;	wait N           do nothing for N frames
;	tell high|low N  wind up, visibly, for N frames - this is the
;	                 warning, and the only warning
;	strike high|low D  the blow; D damage if it is not guarded
;	recover N        open to a counter for N frames
;	goto STATE
;	hurt STATE       go to STATE next time this one is struck
;
; Ironhand is slow and tells for a long time.  He is the one to learn on.

name Ironhand
health 22
reach 46

%

state open
	hurt reel
	wait 50
	tell high 26
	strike high 4
	recover 34
	wait 30
	tell low 26
	strike low 3
	recover 34
	goto open

state reel
	wait 46
	goto open
